                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">759ba0d8-ae8d-4d3a-ae88-45058724013f</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10"></item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">SURFACE TEMPERATURES — ENERGYPLUS
Units: METERS.

*** THE BACKLOG DESCRIPTION OF THIS TEMPLATE IS
WRONG, AND IT MATTERS ***
It calls this a "sibling of SurfaceTemps_FFT.ghx
using SurfaceTemp (EnergyPlus) + SurfaceTemp
Material". Those two components cannot be wired
together. Their signatures share nothing:

  SurfaceTemp (FFT)
    in : EPW, Indoor Temp, MATERIAL, POINTS,
         Run, SKY VIEW, VECTORS
    out: Result  -&gt; Deconstruct SurfaceTemp

  SurfaceTemp (EnergyPlus)
    in : Working Directory, VF MODEL, EPW,
         Settings, Engine, Run
    out: VF Model -&gt; MRT Solve

There is no Material input on the EnergyPlus
variant, and no Points/Sky View/Vectors either.
SurfaceTemp Material is FFT-only. So this is not
a sibling of the FFT template - it is a stage in
the staged MRT view-factor pipeline, which is
what the component's own help says.

THE CHAIN
  MRT Surface (building faces)  ┐
  MRT Surface (ground)          ┴ Merge
                                   |
  MRT Sensors (from Facade Grid) ──┤
                                   v
  MRT View Factors  -&gt; VF Model
                                   v
  SurfaceTemp (EnergyPlus)  -&gt; VF Model with E+
                               temperatures
                                   v
  MRT Solve  -&gt; Probes, Result

Skipping the SurfaceTemp stage leaves every
surface at ambient unless it carries an FFT
temperature from MRT Surface. That is the whole
point of this template.

MRT SETTINGS: EnergyPlus Surfaces is TRUE - that
is the flag that puts the chain on the E+ path.
Radiance Reflections is off so the first run
stays cheap; turn it on for the real study.

GEOMETRY a 10 x 10 x 15 m block on a 40 x 40 m
ground. The block goes through Deconstruct Brep
first: MRT Surface takes Breps, Surfaces or
Meshes, and a Grasshopper Box is none of those -
it reports "No mesh faces produced from the input
geometry". Six faces is also the right granularity
for radiation patches.

SENSOR GRID at 5 m spacing, not 1 m. View factors
are solved probe-to-polygon, so the sweep cost
scales with sensor count; 5 m keeps a template
openable.

THREE RUN TOGGLES, all OFF, left to right:
MRT View Factors, SurfaceTemp (EnergyPlus),
MRT Solve. Click them in that order - each stage
consumes the one before, and the view-factor
sweep is the expensive part, so solving it once
lets the later stages re-run without repeating it.

WORKING DIRECTORY ships as a CHANGE-ME
placeholder. It is a required input, so it cannot
be left blank, and with Run off nothing is
written until you click.

Weather comes from Download Weather as a PATH.
The MRT components take the path directly - they
do NOT need the Weather record component that
Sun Hours and friends require.</item>
                  </items>
